  "worked_solution": "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3-0)^{2}+(-4-(-4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$",
